==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-give chase.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|give<,,gave,given> chase}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To begin [[chase|chasing]] or [[pursue|pursuing]] someone or something, whether on foot or by vehicle.
#: {{syn|en|give pursuit}}
#: {{ux|en|After the robbery, the police '''gave chase''' but didn't catch the suspect.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=22 June 2022|title=Chicago police will no longer be allowed to chase people on foot|work=NPR|url=https://www.npr.org/2022/06/22/1106654201/chicago-police-will-no-longer-be-allowed-to-chase-people-on-foot|text=Under the policy, officers may '''give chase''' if they believe a person is committing or is about to commit a felony, a Class A misdemeanor such as domestic battery, or a serious traffic offense that could risk injuring others, such as drunken driving or street racing.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=30 September 2022|title=Two Drivers Clock Speeds of 150 mph in Georgia Car Chase|work=Yahoo! News|url=https://news.yahoo.com/two-drivers-clock-speeds-150-162537221.html|text=The footage, which was captured at approximately 10:30 pm on September 24, shows two vehicles speeding past the patrol car on Highway 400, prompting the sheriff’s deputy to '''give chase'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=17 January 2023|author=Harry Parker|author2=Rocco Parascandola|author3=Thomas Tracy|title=Wounded NYPD cop '''gave chase''' to Bronx teen accused of shooting him|work=New York Daily News|url=https://www.nydailynews.com/new-york/nyc-crime/ny-bronx-cop-shot-arm-nypd-20230117-zolhppca55hp7cncfiphvcb3wa-story.html|text=An NYPD officer struck in the arm by a bullet allegedly fired by a teen gunman ignored his wound and '''gave chase''' to the 16-year-old suspect, cops said Tuesday.}}

